s generated after the first token. \n“SLA Latency Target Value” is the latency target in Tokens Per Second for a given model as defined by the product documentation.\n“Measured Tokens Per Second” is calculated as either the median (P50) of the Tokens Per Second for each 5 min interval or the average of the Tokens Per Second for each 1 min interval as defined by the product documentation. \n“Excessive Latency Minutes” is the total number of minutes for an Applicable Period during which the Measured Tokens Per Second is less than the SLA Latency Target Value. This excludes intervals where (i) a Request returned an Error Code, (ii) a Request exceeded the Maximum Request Size, or (iii) a Request generated less than 1 token. \n“Excessive Latency Rate” for a given Provisioned Managed Deployment is the sum of Excessive Latency Minutes divided by the total number of minutes in the Applicable Period.  \n“Attainment Percentage” is represented by the following formula: \n\u001a100%-Excessive Latency Rate\u001e\nService Credit:\n\u0010\u0012\u001cAttainment Percentage\n\u001cService Credit\n\u0012\u001c\u003c 99%\n\u001c10%\n\u0011Service Level Exceptions: The Service Credits are only applicable to Azure Direct Models where the SLA Latency Target Value is defined in the product documentation. The Developer tier of the Foundry Models service is not covered by this SLA.\nTable of Contents / Definitions\nObject Replication - Priority Replication\nThis SLA applies to any Replication Policy where the Source Storage Account and Destination Storage Account are located within the same continent and are eligible for Priority Replication.\nAdditional Definitions:\n“Destination Container” is the container which operations are asynchronously replicated to within an Object Replication Policy.\n“Destination Storage Account” is a storage account where operations are asynchronously replicated to, based upon a Replication Policy a user configures with Object Replication on their Source Storage Account.\n“Exceeded Lag Operation” is any operation (data, metadata, properties or deletes) that is pending replication longer than 15 minutes or takes longer than 15 minutes to be replicated from the Source Storage Account to the Destination Storage Account during the billing month.\n“Object Replication” is a storage account feature that asynchronously copies block blobs from a Source Storage Account to a Destination Storage Account. The block blobs within a container are replicated according to Replication Rules a user configures. The contents of the blob, any versions associated with the blob, and the blob\u0027s metadata, properties and deletes are all copied from the Source Container to the Destination Container.\n“Replication Lag” indicates the amount of time that has elapsed between when an operation is performed on the Source Storage Account and when the operation is replicated to the Destination Storage Account.\n“Replication Policy” specifies the Source Storage Account and the Destination Storage Account. A Replication Policy includes one or more rules that specify a Source Container and a Destination Container and indicate which block blobs in the Source Container will be replicated.\n“Replication Rule” specifies how Azure Storage will replicate operations from a Source Container to a Destination Container.\n“Source Container” is the container an operation is originally uploaded to within a Replication Policy.\n"},{"ty":"as","st":"paragraph","si":238285,"ei":238285,"sm":{"ps_klt_i":true,"ps_awao_i":true,"ps_ls":1.0,"ps_sm_i":true,"ps_ls_i":false,"ps_il_i":true,"ps_ir_i":true,"ps_sd":{"sd_bgc2":{"hclr_color":"#ffffff","clr_type":0}},"ps_al_i":true,"ps_bl_i":true,"ps_sd_i":false,"ps_sb_i":true,"ps_lslm_i":true,"ps_br_i":true,"ps_bbtw_i":true,"ps_kwn_i":true,"ps_bt_i":true,"ps_ifl_i":true,"ps_bb_i":true,"ps_pbb_i":true}},{"ty":"as","st":"paragraph","si":238308,"ei":238308,"sm":{"ps_klt_i":true,"ps_awao_i":true,"ps_ls":1.0,"ps_sm_i":true,"ps_ls_i":false,"ps_i